  "articleBody": "Thinking about finishing your garage? It's a great way to add usable space to your home, but there's a bit to think about before you dive in. First off, what's the main purpose of this newly finished space? Is it strictly for parking and storage, or are you dreaming of a dedicated workshop, a hobby zone, or even an extra hang-out spot? Knowing this will guide so many decisions, from insulation needs to the type of flooring you'll want. You'll also need to consider things like whether you’ll need fire-rated separation from your home, or if you'll simply be looking for a cleaner, more finished look. It's not just about aesthetics either; things like local building codes can play a role, especially if you’re making structural changes or adding plumbing or electrical. That’s where a professional can really help you navigate the ins and outs, ensuring everything is up to snuff and will last for years to come. Ultimately, a clear plan prevents headaches down the road. Ready to explore the possibilities for your garage? Give us a call!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
